    ] ;
  skos:definition """The “Vector” class is used to express multi-dimensional quantities with respect to a well defined referenced frame (usually a spatial or spatio-temporal reference frame). This is done by projecting the quantity on one or several axes that define the reference frame and assigning a value to each of the axis projections.

The “Vector” class is a special case of a record that takes a collection of coordinates that are restricted to a numerical representation. """ ;
.
